  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii) — record trip TRP-00410 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-11417: the 2026-08-24T09:10:00+08:00 button-pressed arrival marker was set while the driver's own GPS trace placed him about 850 m from the pickup pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld in full — the $4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on TRP-00410 is refunded and the driver receives no compensation. To the driver: the fee cannot stand, because your own device trace shows you never reached the pickup point and the arrival marker you pressed was false.\n\n1. POL-NS-01 fails. The clause charges a no-show fee only if all four limbs hold. Limbs (a) and (d) do hold: EV-TRIP-00410 records an 'arrived' event at 2026-08-24T09:10:00+08:00 and a driver termination at 09:16:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the codes limb (d) recognises. Limbs (b) and (c) do not. EV-GPS-00410 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0, 84 fixes at 10 s cadence) records 0 of 84 driver fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and a closest approach of 377.4 m, so limb (b) fails. The dwell, measured as limb (c) directs from GPS entry into the geofence, is 0.0 s against the 300 s free-waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 300; the 180 s default would change nothing), so limb (c) fails too. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive: two broken limbs are enough.\n\n2. The arrival marker is false and POL-NS-05 governs. At the 09:10:00 marker the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin — the admissibility pre-pass records every fix from 09:10:00 to 09:16:30 at about 850 m, and the closest approach at any point of the trip is 377.4 m — so the button press did not start the waiting clock. Recomputing the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix yields nothing, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: full refund of the $4.00 cancellation fee, no driver compensation, and a false-arrival record against the driver in the referrals.\n\n3. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result independently: effective dwell 0.0 s against a 300 s minimum is a 300 s shortfall, and limb (i)'s accumulation route is unavailable — the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00410-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), and there are no in-geofence intervals to sum in any event.\n\n4. POL-NS-04 also exonerates the rider: 'where are you? im at the block' was sent at 09:12:00 inside the waiting window (limb (a)); no chat reply came within 120 seconds and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, the driver cancelling 270 seconds later (limb (b)); and the rider track places her within the 100 m STANDARD presence radius on all 44 qualifying fixes, mean 14.6 m, maximum 19.1 m (limb (c)).\n\n5. Arguments rejected. (i) The record's own 390-second clock (09:10:00 to 09:16:30) does not satisfy limb (c): POL-NS-01(c) expressly measures the dwell from GPS entry into the geofence, not from the arrival tap, and the trace never enters it. (ii) The system chat message 'Your driver has arrived' at 09:10:01 (EV-CHAT-00410, weight 1.0) is not a second, independent carrier of the arrival fact: it is generated from the same button press, and if the instrument evidence were removed it would support nothing, so it is a restatement and does not lift the POL-GEN-02(2) cap to 1.0. (iii) The SGD 3.20 driver compensation (derived.money.driver_compensation) is conditional on POL-NS-01 being satisfied in full, which it is not. (iv) The anti-farming check is passed — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/120 = 0.008 (not above 0.08) — so nothing is withheld on that ground and POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged by it. (v) POL-NS-03 does not take over: it requires a stationary dwell of 300 s within 400 m of the pin, and the 377.4 m figure is a moving approach, not a dwell; registered_pickup_points is 1, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises either. (vi) Escalation under POL-NS-09(b) is declined. That trigger requires that no clause resolve the trip-record/trace conflict, and POL-NS-05 resolves it by testing and falsifying the button-pressed marker; POL-NS-12 is not open (it covers GPS_AUTO arrivals only, and this marker is BUTTON), and POL-NS-09(a), (c) and (e) are not engaged.\n\n6. Weight and confidence. EV-TRIP-00410 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, and both sides disclosed it as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. The tag is schema-level: it meets none of POL-NS-08's limbs (a) to (d) — the 09:10:00 event matches a trace fix to within seconds, the trace has no gap over 120 s and carries 84 fixes, the chat holds exactly the 2 messages the trip record counts, and the $4.00 fare line equals the cancellation fee in force ($4.00, identical to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd). It is therefore down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only and does not decide the case: the deciding facts are the driver's position (EV-GPS-00410, weight 1.0) and the fee charged (EV-FARE-00410, weight 1.0), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no POL-NS-08 closing-sentence escalation applies. Confidence 0.90.\n\nThe monetary effect, $4.00, is below the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes automatically on issue; both parties may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
