{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii) — false-arrival record: record trip TRP-00410 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-11417. The 'arrived' marker was pressed at 2026-08-24T09:10:00+08:00 while the driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00410) placed him 377.4 m from the pickup pin, and the trace contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To rider RDR-11692 and driver DRV-11417: the $4.00 cancellation fee charged on 24 Aug 2026 is refunded in full to the rider, and nothing is paid to the driver.\n\nWHAT THE EVIDENCE SHOWS. The driver's own device trace (EV-GPS-00410, admissibility COMPLETE, weight 1.0) runs from acceptance at 09:02:35 to cancellation at 09:16:30, 84 fixes at 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps. It never once places the driver inside the 50 m arrival radius for this STANDARD pickup: 0 of 84 fixes qualify under the 25 m accuracy filter, and his closest approach at any point in the whole trace is 377.4 m from the pin. Under POL-NS-02 that means no admissible arrival and a failure of POL-NS-01 limb (b), so the fee is not chargeable. The button-pressed 'arrived' marker at 09:10:00 is likewise FALSE under POL-NS-05, because at that timestamp the trace places the driver more than 300 m away; recomputing the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix yields no such fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies — full refund, no compensation, and the trip is recorded against the driver as a false arrival (see referrals). Independently, the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 300), a 300-second shortfall, so POL-NS-06 also requires the full refund. POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider as well: she sent a locating message, 'where are you? im at the block', at 09:12:00 (EV-CHAT-00410, weight 1.0), received no reply and no in-app call before the 09:16:30 cancellation, and her device sat within the 100 m rider-presence radius on all 44 qualifying fixes (mean 14.6 m, maximum 19.1 m).\n\nTHE IMPAIRED RECORD, AND THE DRIVER'S ARGUMENTS. EV-TRIP-00410 is impaired (weight 0.4, issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT): it records an arrival at 09:10:00 and a 6.5-minute wait while the trace holds every fix in that same interval hundreds of metres away. That impairment is disclosed, and it is why the record cannot carry the charge: its arrival event and its RIDER_NO_SHOW termination are literally recorded (POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d)), but POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and limbs (b) and (c) fail on the clean trace, so the driver's claim that the fee stands fails. The 390-second dwell the driver's advocate computes runs from the arrival tap, but POL-NS-01(c) measures the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, and there is none — the measured dwell is 0.0 seconds, not 390. I do not accept that the system message 'Your driver has arrived' (09:10:01) is a second, independent carrier of the arrival: it is the platform's relay of the very same arrival tap recorded in EV-TRIP-00410, so it fails the removal test and the two are one carrier, not two. That does not change the outcome, because confidence is capped by the artifact that actually carries the deciding fact — the driver's position over the waiting window — and that is EV-GPS-00410 at weight 1.0, an artifact under no impairment. The POL-GEN-02(2) cap on this ruling is therefore 1.0, and my confidence is 0.9. POL-NS-08's escalation sentence is not engaged either: the trip record's tag is a schema-level conflict, not an impairment under POL-NS-08 limbs (a)–(d) — the arrival event matches a GPS fix to within 5 seconds, the trace has no gap longer than 120 seconds, the chat log matches the trip record's chat_message_count of 2, and the $4.00 ledger line reconciles with the $4.00 fee in force.\n\nESCALATION IS NOT REQUIRED. The driver's advocate asks for escalation under POL-NS-09(b). But the conflict is resolved by a clause: POL-NS-05 tests the button-pressed marker against the trace and falsifies it, and POL-NS-12 — the one route that could have rehabilitated a platform-confirmed arrival — expressly does not cover a BUTTON marker, which is what this trip's platform_policy.arrival_marker is. No other limb of POL-NS-09 fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, both profiles show 0 disputes between these parties in the last 90 days, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below 0.08), so no compensation is withheld on that ground. The driver's advocate is right about the anti-farming figures, but they only matter if compensation were otherwise due, and it is not.\n\nTHE MONEY. The ledger (EV-FARE-00410) shows $4.00 charged (total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED) and nothing returned (refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The rider gets that $4.00 cancellation-fee line back — the full contested amount. No compensation is payable to the driver: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and here POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 all displace it, so the $3.20 the ledger derives is not triggered. Even on the wrong-entrance reading POL-NS-03 would fund no payment: registered_pickup_points is 1, so limb (ii) goodwill cannot arise, and the rider did name her block in the chat without the driver moving to it, which is limb (i)'s no-compensation case. The only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00410-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06 limb (i) accumulation could not be used in any event — and with 0 in-geofence intervals there was nothing to accumulate. The monetary effect ($4.00) is below the $8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05 (general policy), so this refund executes on issue; this is a provisional automated ruling and either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
